---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CaseHero from '../components/CaseHero.astro';
import Module from '../components/Module.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import MoreWork from '../components/MoreWork.astro';
import Decisions from '../components/Decisions.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import { getProject } from '../data/projects';
import hero from '../assets/schwab-trading/hero.png';
import responsive from '../assets/schwab-trading/responsive-behavior.png';
import responsiveDark from '../assets/schwab-trading/responsive-behavior-dark.png';
import modules from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-modules.png';
import modulesDark from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-modules-dark.png';
import whiteboard from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-whiteboard.png';
import whiteboardDark from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-whiteboard-dark.png';
import desktop from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-desktop.png';
import desktopDark from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-desktop-dark.png';
import tablet from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-tablet.png';
import tabletDark from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-tablet-dark.png';
import mobile from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-mobile.png';
import mobileDark from '../assets/schwab-trading/panel-mobile-dark.png';

const p = getProject('project-5-schwab-trading');
---
<Base title={`${p.title} | Jeremy Hamann`} description={p.description}>
  <div class="case">
    <div class="top">
      <CaseHero project={p} image={hero} bg="var(--hero-schwab)" artWidth={357} textWidth={414} alt="Schwab trading research platform" />

      <Module title="Lay of the Land" icon="target_check">
        <p>In late 2020 I joined the team helping bring Charles Schwab’s new retail trading research experience out of beta phase. The research section of Schwab’s retail trading platform is used by customers all over the world to help them make wise trading decisions. I led the design of 30+ trading research modules’ responsive behaviors.</p>
      </Module>

      <Decisions items={[
        { title: 'Work module by module, with stakeholder sign-off on each', constraint: '30+ data-heavy modules and a fixed launch window.', tradeoff: 'More reviews along the way, but development could build each module as soon as it was approved.' },
        { title: 'Codify responsive rules, not just one-off layouts', constraint: 'New modules would keep coming after launch.', tradeoff: 'Upfront effort to document a ruleset, so future modules follow it without starting from zero.' },
        { title: 'Let simple tables scroll, and give complex charts their own treatment', constraint: 'Non-professional traders need usable data on every screen size.', tradeoff: 'Tables keep their full data with a horizontal scroll, while charts get a more tailored layout per screen size to stay usable.' },
      ]} />

      <Module title="Success" icon="sports_score">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>After a successful release from beta into full production, Schwab has implemented the experience on their retail trading research site.</p>
          <p>As a result of creating a set of responsive guidelines, Schwab will be able to continue to design modules that are useful no matter the screen size.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Created responsive designs for each research platform module</li>
            <li>Led collaborative design consistency workshops</li>
            <li>Led weekly design reviews with Schwab’s business stakeholders, internal design teams and developers</li>
            <li>Provided continual support for the Schwab engineering team during the development cycle leading to deployment</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </Module>
    </div>

    <Panel src={responsive} srcDark={responsiveDark} alt="A research module at desktop, tablet and mobile widths" caption="Responsive behavior of Schwab’s trading research platform" />

    <Module title="The challenge" icon="swords" id="challenge">
      <p>Our task was to help the Schwab team establish a coherent responsivity ruleset for a wide variety of informational modules. We needed to get stakeholder buy-in on each module's viability so that development could create these modules in the allotted timeframe before launch.</p>
    </Module>
    <Module title="Approach" icon="switch_access_2">
      <p>Based on Schwab stakeholders' goals (make this happen as fast as possible) and timeframe we took a module-by-module approach to tackling each different circumstance of responsive design. We worked together with Schwab’s stakeholders and internal design team to verify each module’s viability in terms of usability and scope of development.</p>
    </Module>
    <Module title="Research" icon="search">
      <p>As a part of our initial design approach we conducted a competitive analysis of other banks' and brokerages' responsive designs to determine a best-practice approach.</p>
    </Module>

    <Panel src={modules} srcDark={modulesDark} alt="A collage of research modules" caption="A small selection of the 30+ responsive modules needed for the platform" />

    <Module title="Creatively Working Together" icon="groups" id="working-together">
      <p>As our team encountered each new responsive challenge we began to compile a working list of our rulesets. We used InVision whiteboard to collect, categorize and consistently bounce each of these responsive rulesets off of Schwab stakeholders and their own internal design team. Our stakeholders were wowed and loved the flexibility and clarity a tool like a digital whiteboard gave to the process.</p>
    </Module>

    <Panel src={whiteboard} srcDark={whiteboardDark} alt="Whiteboard of responsive rulesets" caption="Whiteboard workshops with stakeholders helped us to develop guidelines depending on the module/data type." />

    <Module title="Coherence & Complexity" icon="grid_goldenratio" id="coherence">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Various tables, charts, graphs, and visualizations all needed a unique design touch. Some modules were just simple tables that could easily use wrapped content with a scroll. Others, like complex charting, needed a more nuanced touch to maintain usability.</p>
        <p>Our design work was not only in creating various configurations of data visualization that fit multiple screen sizes, but also in codifying and implementing comprehensive responsivity guidelines that applied to all modules across the Schwab Retail Research website (now and into the future). These guidelines needed to take into account potentially complex data displayed in various ways including tabular data and charting of various kinds. Because the site is a retail trading platform, usability was also paramount to the non-professional traders who use it.</p>
      </div>
    </Module>

    <div class="bands">
      <Panel src={desktop} srcDark={desktopDark} alt="A module at desktop width" caption="Desktop" gap={8} />
      <Panel src={tablet} srcDark={tabletDark} alt="A module at tablet width" caption="Tablet" gap={8} />
      <Panel src={mobile} srcDark={mobileDark} alt="A module at mobile width" caption="Mobile" gap={8} />
    </div>

    <Module title="Results" icon="sports_score">
      <p>Beyond the 30+ modules shipped, the lasting result is the guideline set itself: a documented, reusable rule set that Schwab’s designers and developers can apply to every future module, whatever the data type or screen size.</p>
    </Module>

    <ContactCTA />

    <MoreWork slugs={['project-2-commsec', 'project-1-seven-post-client-portal']} />
  </div>
</Base>
